<item>
  <title>Your first steps in R: from numbers to a chart</title>
  <dc:creator>The Tanzanian R Users team</dc:creator>
  <link>https://r-users-tz.github.io/posts/2026-11-13-first-steps-in-r/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 





<p>This tutorial is for people who have <strong>never used R before</strong>. By the end you’ll have written a few lines of code, summarised a small table of data and drawn a chart. It takes about 30 minutes.</p>
<section id="install-r-and-an-editor" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="install-r-and-an-editor">1. Install R and an editor</h2>
<p>You need two free programs:</p>
<ol type="1">
<li><strong>R</strong>, the language itself. Download it from <a href="https://cran.r-project.org/">CRAN</a> and choose Windows, macOS or Linux.</li>
<li><strong>An editor</strong> to write code in. Most beginners use <a href="https://posit.co/download/rstudio-desktop/">RStudio Desktop</a>. <a href="https://positron.posit.co/">Positron</a> is a newer alternative from the same company.</li>
</ol>
<p>Install R first, then the editor. Open the editor and find the <strong>Console</strong>: that’s where you type the code below and press <strong>Enter</strong> to run it.</p>
<div class="callout callout-style-default callout-tip callout-titled">
<div class="callout-header d-flex align-content-center">
<div class="callout-icon-container">
<i class="callout-icon"></i>
</div>
<div class="callout-title-container flex-fill">
<span class="screen-reader-only">Tip</span>No computer, or can’t install software?
</div>
</div>
<div class="callout-body-container callout-body">
<p><a href="https://posit.cloud/">Posit Cloud</a> runs RStudio in your web browser. The free plan is enough for this tutorial.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="r-as-a-calculator" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="r-as-a-calculator">2. R as a calculator</h2>
<p>R can do arithmetic, just like a calculator:</p>
<div class="cell">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb1" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode r code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb1-1"><span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">2</span> <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">+</span> <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">3</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<div class="cell-output cell-output-stdout">
<pre><code>[1] 5</code></pre>
</div>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb3" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode r code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb3-1"><span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">1500</span> <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">*</span> <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">12</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<div class="cell-output cell-output-stdout">
<pre><code>[1] 18000</code></pre>
</div>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb5" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode r code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb5-1">(<span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">42000</span> <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">+</span> <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">38500</span>) <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">/</span> <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">2</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<div class="cell-output cell-output-stdout">
<pre><code>[1] 40250</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="saving-values-with--" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="saving-values-with--">3. Saving values with <code>&lt;-</code></h2>
<p>To keep a value for later, give it a name with the arrow <code>&lt;-</code>. Read it as “gets”:</p>
<div class="cell">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb7" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode r code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb7-1">price_per_kg <span class="ot" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&lt;-</span> <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">2500</span>      <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># price of 1 kg of maize flour, in TZS</span></span>
<span id="cb7-2">kilos_sold <span class="ot" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&lt;-</span> <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">18</span></span>
<span id="cb7-3"></span>
<span id="cb7-4">price_per_kg <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">*</span> kilos_sold</span></code></pre></div></div>
<div class="cell-output cell-output-stdout">
<pre><code>[1] 45000</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Names can contain letters, numbers, <code>_</code> and <code>.</code>, but can’t start with a number. Anything after <code>#</code> is a <strong>comment</strong>: R ignores it, but it helps people reading your code.</p>
</section>
<section id="many-values-at-once-vectors" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="many-values-at-once-vectors">4. Many values at once: vectors</h2>
<p>A <strong>vector</strong> holds several values of the same kind. Create one with <code>c()</code>, which stands for “combine”. Here are a week of maize flour sales from a small duka (shop), Monday to Sunday:</p>
<div class="cell">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb9" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode r code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb9-1">maize_sales <span class="ot" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">c</span>(<span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">42000</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">38500</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">45000</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">40000</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">51000</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">63000</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">57000</span>)</span>
<span id="cb9-2"></span>
<span id="cb9-3"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">sum</span>(maize_sales)    <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># total for the week</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<div class="cell-output cell-output-stdout">
<pre><code>[1] 336500</code></pre>
</div>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb11" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode r code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb11-1"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">mean</span>(maize_sales)   <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># average per day</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<div class="cell-output cell-output-stdout">
<pre><code>[1] 48071.43</code></pre>
</div>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb13" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode r code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb13-1"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">max</span>(maize_sales)    <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># best day</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<div class="cell-output cell-output-stdout">
<pre><code>[1] 63000</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><code>sum()</code>, <code>mean()</code> and <code>max()</code> are <strong>functions</strong>: you give them something inside the brackets and they give you an answer back.</p>
<div class="callout callout-style-default callout-note callout-titled">
<div class="callout-header d-flex align-content-center">
<div class="callout-icon-container">
<i class="callout-icon"></i>
</div>
<div class="callout-title-container flex-fill">
Note
</div>
</div>
<div class="callout-body-container callout-body">
<p>The shop and its numbers are made up for this tutorial.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="tables-of-data-data-frames" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="tables-of-data-data-frames">5. Tables of data: data frames</h2>
<p>Real data usually comes as a table, with rows and columns. In R a table is called a <strong>data frame</strong>. Let’s record a week of sales for three products:</p>
<div class="cell">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb15" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode r code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb15-1">sales <span class="ot" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">data.frame</span>(</span>
<span id="cb15-2">  <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">day =</span> <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">rep</span>(<span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">c</span>(<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Mon"</span>, <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Tue"</span>, <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Wed"</span>, <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Thu"</span>, <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Fri"</span>, <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Sat"</span>, <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Sun"</span>), <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">times =</span> <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">3</span>),</span>
<span id="cb15-3">  <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">product =</span> <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">rep</span>(<span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">c</span>(<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Maize flour"</span>, <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Cooking oil"</span>, <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Sugar"</span>), <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">each =</span> <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">7</span>),</span>
<span id="cb15-4">  <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">amount_tzs =</span> <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">c</span>(</span>
<span id="cb15-5">    <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">42000</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">38500</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">45000</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">40000</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">51000</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">63000</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">57000</span>,  <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># maize flour</span></span>
<span id="cb15-6">    <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">25000</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">27500</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">24000</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">26000</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">31000</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">39000</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">34500</span>,  <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># cooking oil</span></span>
<span id="cb15-7">    <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">18000</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">16500</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">19500</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">17000</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">22000</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">28500</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">25000</span>   <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># sugar</span></span>
<span id="cb15-8">  )</span>
<span id="cb15-9">)</span>
<span id="cb15-10"></span>
<span id="cb15-11"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">head</span>(sales)   <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># show the first six rows</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<div class="cell-output cell-output-stdout">
<pre><code>  day     product amount_tzs
1 Mon Maize flour      42000
2 Tue Maize flour      38500
3 Wed Maize flour      45000
4 Thu Maize flour      40000
5 Fri Maize flour      51000
6 Sat Maize flour      63000</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><code>rep()</code> repeats values, so we don’t have to type every day and product by hand. In practice you would usually read a table from a file, for example with <code>read.csv("sales.csv")</code>.</p>
</section>
<section id="add-on-packages" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="add-on-packages">6. Add-on packages</h2>
<p>Thousands of free <strong>packages</strong> add extra features to R. Two of the most popular are <strong>dplyr</strong>, for working with tables, and <strong>ggplot2</strong>, for charts. Install them once:</p>
<div class="cell">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb17" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode r code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb17-1"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">install.packages</span>(<span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">c</span>(<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"dplyr"</span>, <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"ggplot2"</span>))</span></code></pre></div></div>
</div>
<p>Then load them each time you start R:</p>
<div class="cell">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb18" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode r code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb18-1"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">library</span>(dplyr)</span>
<span id="cb18-2"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">library</span>(ggplot2)</span></code></pre></div></div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="summarise-the-week" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="summarise-the-week">7. Summarise the week</h2>
<p>With dplyr we can ask: <em>how much did each product earn this week, and which was its best day?</em></p>
<div class="cell">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb19" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode r code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb19-1">weekly <span class="ot" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&lt;-</span> sales <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">|&gt;</span></span>
<span id="cb19-2">  <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">group_by</span>(product) <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">|&gt;</span></span>
<span id="cb19-3">  <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">summarise</span>(</span>
<span id="cb19-4">    <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">total_tzs =</span> <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">sum</span>(amount_tzs),</span>
<span id="cb19-5">    <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">best_day =</span> day[<span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">which.max</span>(amount_tzs)]</span>
<span id="cb19-6">  ) <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">|&gt;</span></span>
<span id="cb19-7">  <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">arrange</span>(<span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">desc</span>(total_tzs))</span>
<span id="cb19-8"></span>
<span id="cb19-9">weekly</span></code></pre></div></div>
<div class="cell-output cell-output-stdout">
<pre><code># A tibble: 3 × 3
  product     total_tzs best_day
  &lt;chr&gt;           &lt;dbl&gt; &lt;chr&gt;   
1 Maize flour    336500 Sat     
2 Cooking oil    207000 Sat     
3 Sugar          146500 Sat     </code></pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Read the <code>|&gt;</code> symbol (the <strong>pipe</strong>) as “and then”: take <code>sales</code>, <em>and then</em> group it by product, <em>and then</em> summarise each group, <em>and then</em> sort from largest to smallest.</p>
<p>Altogether, the shop took in <strong>TZS 690,000</strong> this week, and Saturday was the busiest day for every product.</p>
</section>
<section id="your-first-chart" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="your-first-chart">8. Your first chart</h2>
<p>Finally, let’s draw it. ggplot2 builds a chart in layers, joined with <code>+</code>:</p>
<div class="cell">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb21" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode r code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb21-1"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">ggplot</span>(weekly, <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">aes</span>(<span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">x =</span> total_tzs, <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">y =</span> <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">reorder</span>(product, total_tzs))) <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">+</span></span>
<span id="cb21-2">  <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">geom_col</span>(<span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">fill =</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"#0B6E2E"</span>, <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">width =</span> <span class="fl" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">0.6</span>) <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">+</span></span>
<span id="cb21-3">  <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
