<p>Line by line:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>ggplot(weekly, aes(...))</code> chooses the data and what goes on each axis. <code>reorder()</code> sorts the bars by size.</li>
<li><code>geom_col()</code> draws the bars.</li>
<li><code>geom_text()</code> writes each total next to its bar.</li>
<li><code>scale_x_continuous()</code> adds commas to the numbers on the axis.</li>
<li><code>labs()</code> sets the title and axis labels.</li>
<li><code>theme_minimal()</code> and <code>theme()</code> give it a clean look.</li>
</ul>
<p>Try changing the colour <code>"#0B6E2E"</code> or the title, then run the code again.</p>
</section>
<section id="what-next" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="what-next">What next?</h2>
<p>Congratulations, you’ve written your first R code! To keep going:</p>
<ul>
<li>Work through the free book <a href="https://r4ds.hadley.nz/">R for Data Science</a>, the standard next step.</li>
<li>Browse our <a href="../../resources.html">learning resources</a>, including Tanzanian data sources to practise on.</li>
<li><a href="../../join.html">Join the community</a> and come to a meetup. Bring your questions.</li>
</ul>
<p>Stuck? Ask in our community channels. Everyone was a beginner once.</p>


</section>

